From 16b88ddf1b13a600039f09854ec5a942276532d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JoshuaHayesWasHere <josh.hayes121@icloud.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 01:10:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): a jstack child home pins open in the tree, and its
 row sums up its tasks by stage in place of a word on each task's row

A child home's menu has Pin open and Unpin, and a pin at its row's end does the same. A pinned
home stays unfolded, idle or live, never faded, with a filled pin, kept in the client settings
(jstackTreePinnedHomes) so it lasts across a reload; T3's own thread pins are apart.

The home row says what is under it, folded or open, such as "2 scouts, 5 review, 1 queued", in
place of its age, and the tally line under a folded home is gone. A task's row is bare but for
"asks you" and a stalled, quiet or held wait; where it stands is in its tooltip, heads its menu,
and is said to a screen reader.
